<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marion Mahony Griffin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1871">1871</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marion Mahony Griffin was an American architect and artist, among the first women licensed as architects in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and an early member of Frank Lloyd Wright's studio. Her striking drawings presented the plan for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canberra">Canberra</a> with which her husband and partner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-burley-griffin">Walter Burley Griffin</a> won the international competition in 1912. She worked with him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marion-mahony-griffin.jpg" alt="Marion Mahony Griffin" width="116" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walterburleygriffin_(cropped)2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
